{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["The reason for <b>ki tistarer aleinu gam histarer</b> — \"even many dominions,\" or \"you and Aaron your brother.\" This is the language of Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Numbers 16:13). In my opinion, <b>gam</b> in this place has the meaning of \"even,\" as in \"there is none, not even one\" (Psalms 14:3), \"even to his neighbor a poor man is hated\" (Proverbs 20), and similar verses. They said: Is it too little for you that you have done great evil with us to put us to death in the wilderness — for we would have been worthy to stone you — that you exercise dominion over us even a minimal dominion, to send us to go up before you?! All the more so that you should rule and exalt yourself over us!"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:05.704149361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}